snippet.description:
In September 1666, a small fire started inside a bakery on Pudding Lane… but within hours, it turned into one of the most devastating disasters in history.

The Great Fire of London burned for four days, destroying over 13,000 homes, churches, and landmarks — including the famous Old St. Paul’s Cathedral. With no fire brigade and strong winds spreading the flames, the entire city faced chaos, panic, and destruction.

In this short historical documentary, discover the real story behind the Great Fire of London — how it started, why it spread so rapidly, and how this tragedy reshaped one of the world’s greatest cities forever.

🔥 Watch till the end to see how London rose again from the ashes.

